This directory exists so importlib.metadata can resolve the vendored
splunklib's own version. splunklib 3.0's binding.py calls
importlib.metadata.version("splunk-sdk") to build its User-Agent header, which
raises PackageNotFoundError when the library is vendored into an app's bin/
directory rather than pip-installed. Shipping the package metadata fixes that
without patching vendored third-party code, which would otherwise have to be
re-applied on every SDK upgrade.
